<title>UK: Scholl underlying first half profits edge up.</title>
<headline>Scholl underlying first half profits edge up.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		11.5		   vs 10.0</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 3.0		    vs *</p>
<p> Pretax, pre-exceps     13.79		  vs 11.79</p>
<p> Turnover		   119.39		 vs 109.70</p>
<p> Operating result	 13.89		  vs 12.11</p>
<p> Exceptionals (net)     29.39 charge	 vs nil</p>
<p> Interest		   0.69		   vs 0.43</p>
<p> Tax			  1.76 credit	  vs 3.72 charge</p>
<p> Net taxed		  20.14 loss	   vs 8.08 profit</p>
<p> Retaind		    23.61 loss	   vs 4.82 profit</p>
<p> Pay date		   n/a</p>
<p> Div registration date  n/a</p>
<p> Ex-div date		n/a</p>
<p>NOTE - Footwear specialist Scholl Plc said the 29.4 million stg exceptional charge was in connection with restructuring. Earnings per share are excluding exceptional items.</p>
<p>Chairman Stuart Wallis said that &quot;trading in the second half of the year has so far maintained the strong performance of the first six months and I am positive about the outcome for the full year.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 5427717</p>
